      <floats-group id="article-26448.s7">
        <fig id="article-26448.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Mature Ovarian Follicle. The image depicts a mature ovarian follicle, also known as a Graafian follicle. In this stage, the oocyte has completed the first meiotic division (2N haploid) and is surrounded by granulosa cells. The cavity formed in the middle is known as the follicular antrum. The antrum contains hyaluronic acid and proteoglycans. The theca interna, a layer of cells surrounding the follicle, produces estrogen. Upon ovulation, the oocyte is released into the oviduct&#x000a0; (hematoxylin-eosin, original magnification &#x000d7;4). Contributed by F Farci, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="follicolo001" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
